The charts vendor no third-party templates or subcharts. The one subchart,
cart (pulled into sglang and vllm through file://../cart), is in this
repository. The llmscaleoperator chart was generated from the ModelSphere
llm-operator repository with the kubebuilder Helm plugin, and the CRDs in
autoconfig and llmscaleoperator are generated by controller-gen from
ModelSphere sources.

Container images
  The charts reference container images; they neither contain nor
  redistribute them. Each image is pulled from its registry at install time
  and is under its own licenses.

  ModelSphere images (Docker Hub, 4pdosc/), built and published by the
  organization's repositories at https://github.com/modelsphere: autoconfig,
  cache_aware_router, hang-watcher, llm-openresty (the OpenResty router and
  the body-log images), llm-operator, slo-api, slo-scaler-decision-gen.
  Their own NOTICE files list what they contain.

  Third-party images the charts default to
    lmsysorg/sglang ............. SGLang engine (sglang chart)
    vllm/vllm-openai ............ vLLM engine (vllm chart)
    hashicorp/http-echo ......... scaling mock in the sglang and vllm charts,
                                  only with metricsMock.enabled (off by default)

rdma-injector image (charts/rdma-injector/image, 4pdosc/rdma-injector)
  Built from this repository. The webhook uses only the Python standard
  library; the Dockerfile builds on docker.io/library/python
  (python:3.12-alpine) -- see that image's own licenses.
